d correspond to customers. We need attribute orders to current member level. If multiple members same customer_unique_id could duplicate orders. But data contract? The reference example does join without dedup. Use same pattern. Need output level_id and amount rounded two. Might not need member_levels because output level ID. Only level_id from members. SQL:\n\nSELECT m.level_id, ROUND(SUM(oi.price), 2) AS total_amount\nFROM members m\nJOIN customers c ON c.customer_unique_id = m.customer_unique_id\nJOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id\nJOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\nGROUP BY m.level_id\nORDER BY m.level_id;\n\nNeed LIMIT? Rule 3: must LIMIT except single-row no GROUP BY count/sum/avg. This has GROUP BY, so need LIMIT. Add LIMIT 100? TopN? Not specified; default need limit. Could add LIMIT 1000 or 20. Since levels likely few. Use LIMIT 100. But final maybe \"LIMIT 20\" not specified. Any LIMIT to satisfy. Since no sorting specified, maybe ORDER BY level_id. Limit 100. Rule \"直接输出可执行 SQL, no code fence\".\n\nNeed consider \"全部订单状态下\" all statuses: no status filter. \"商品金额合计，不含运费或支付金额\" sum oi.price not freight nor payment. Good.\n\nNeed maybe use DISTINCT order item? order_items primary (order_id, order_item_id), each row item. Fine.\n\nPotential issue if a member has no orders? \"这些会员\" could include members without orders, but sum for all members by level? \"统计这些会员全部订单状态下的商品金额合计\" likely members with orders. If include no orders, SUM null; not needed. INNER joins.\n\nNeed think \"当前会员等级ID\" maybe current level is members.level_id. Output level ID and amount two decimals. Yes.\n\nNeed not include level name. Good.\n\nNeed no explanatory comment? Rule 18 allows comment for complex multi-table; but simpler. Only output SQL.\n\nNeed decide order by. We can sort by level_id. With limit. Use ROUND(SUM(oi.price), 2). Since SUM numeric, okay. Alias maybe total_amount. \n\nNeed ensure table/columns lowercase. Good.\n\nLet's final."},"logprobs":nu